# GitHub Workflow Orchestration

Follow after local agent phases complete (see `workflow-orchestration.mdc`). Use `rtk gh` / `rtk git` for GitHub operations.

## Branch model (main → develop → feature)

```
main          production-ready; tag releases here
  ↑
develop       integration branch; default base for daily work
  ↑
feature/*     short-lived work branches
```

| Branch | Purpose | Rules |
|--------|---------|-------|
| `main` | Production | Protected — never force-push; merge from `develop` (release) or `hotfix/*` only |
| `develop` | Integration | Default checkout for new work; CI must pass before merging features |
| `feature/*` | New work | Branch **from `develop`**; PR **into `develop`** |

### Branch naming

```bash
feature/<scope>-<short-name>   # e.g. feature/phase-3-inventory
fix/<scope>-<short-name>       # bugfix → develop
hotfix/<scope>-<short-name>    # urgent prod fix → main (+ back-merge to develop)
chore/<short-name>             # tooling/docs → develop
```

### Daily flow

```bash
rtk git checkout develop && rtk git pull
rtk git checkout -b feature/phase-3-inventory
# … implement, test, commit …
rtk git push -u origin HEAD
rtk gh pr create --base develop --head feature/phase-3-inventory
```

Release: open PR `develop` → `main` after phase gate + CI green. Never commit directly to `main` or `develop`.

## PR phase gate

Do not open a PR until:

- `docs/prd/<feature>.md` (or approved foundation docs)
- `docs/architecture/<feature>.md`
- `docs/design/<feature>.md` (UI changes)
- `test-engineer` report mapped to P0 criteria

## PR body template

```markdown
## Summary
- <1-3 bullets describing why>

## Docs
- <paths to prd/architecture/design touched>

## Test plan
- [ ] <checklist mapped to P0 acceptance criteria>
```

## CI expectations

1. **Lint** — ESLint, Prettier, typecheck
2. **Test** — unit + API integration + Playwright smoke
3. **Build** — all apps and packages compile

Block merge if any check fails. Never `git push --force` to `main` or `develop`.

## Commit policy

- Conventions: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `test:`
- Only create commits when the user explicitly requests

## Handoff block

```
## GitHub Handoff
- **Branch**: feature/... (base: develop)
- **PR**: <url or ready to open> → develop
- **CI**: pending | green | failed
- **Docs**: docs/prd/..., docs/architecture/..., docs/design/...
```
